## Tests import and exercise the code under test
A test of a local copy or a standard-library stand-in keeps passing when the real module is broken or deleted.
```python
# bad
def apply_discount(price, percent):  # pasted copy of pricing.apply_discount
    return price * (100 - percent) / 100

def test_apply_discount():
    assert apply_discount(200, 10) == 180
```
```python
# good
from pricing import apply_discount

def test_apply_discount():
    assert apply_discount(200, 10) == 180
```
